arning(...); return` — the OptionalDependencyError is swallowed.","push.py:646-651 docstring: push_after_commit is the auto-push for transition/reopen/claim/compact/delete which 'do their own locked rename+commit rather than going through write_and_push'."],"finding":"push_after_commit — the auto-push caller for the inline-commit write paths (transition/reopen/claim via txn.py, compact via compact.py, delete via delete.py) — calls push_tickets_branch inside a `try/except Exception` that swallows the raise and only logs a warning, so the S3 preflight's OptionalDependencyError (raised INSIDE push_tickets_branch per the plan) will be caught and swallowed on those paths, defeating the fail-closed contract. The plan enumerates only write_and_push (which does NOT catch) and never mentions push_after_commit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce03e85eb6ff6b30","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'The best-effort contract, resolved explicitly.'; push.py:646-668 push_after_commit","norm_id":"nd157400f7a8081b2","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A trailing `rebar transition`/`compact`/`delete`/`claim` against an s3:// remote with the helper missing: the local commit lands, push_after_commit swallows the OptionalDependencyError, and the unlocked corrupting push proceeds / no actionable message surfaces."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either let push_after_commit re-raise OptionalDependencyError (catch it specifically before the broad except and re-raise), or run _require_s3_helper_if_s3_url on the resolved remote before entering push_after_commit's try; and add these inline-commit paths to the scope + test oracles.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"high","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the full set of `push_tickets_branch` auto-push call sites via find_referencing_symbols (not just write_and_push@587): enumerate push_after_commit (push.py:663, which catches Exception and would SWALLOW the S3 error — reconcile or exempt it), batch_write_and_push (event_append.py:617), and import_ndjson.py:381, and state which propagate the preflight raise vs. swallow it.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: \"its auto-push callers (`write_and_push` at `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:587`) call it **without** a try/except\"","src/rebar/_store/push.py:663 push_after_commit: `push_tickets_branch(canonical)` inside `try: ... except Exception: logger.warning(...)` — swallows OptionalDependencyError","src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:617 batch_write_and_push and src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:381 are additional un-enumerated auto-push callers"],"finding":"The plan enumerates the auto-push callers of `push_tickets_branch` that call it without a try/except as only `write_and_push` (event_append.py:587), but this call-site inventory is incomplete. A grep sweep for `push_tickets_branch` surfaces `push_after_commit` (push.py:663), which wraps the call 